;; macOS sandbox profile for the strategy subprocess.
;;
;; `sandbox-exec(1)` is documented as deprecated and has been for a decade; it
;; is still present and still enforcing on macOS 15.0 / arm64, which is what the
;; spike measured. Deprecated-but-working is the honest description, and it is
;; the reason the recommendation is that scored runs happen on Linux.
;;
;; Read is allowed: the child imports Python, the stdlib and src.core.types.
;; Everything that could exfiltrate or persist is denied.
(version 1)
(allow default)

;; finding 7's prevention half: the null tables, the calendar, the ledger and
;; the strategy's own source all live on this filesystem.
(deny file-write*)

;; a strategy that can open a socket can publish its score, fetch a future bar,
;; or ask something else to run for it.
(deny network*)

;; and it must not be able to step outside the sandbox by exec'ing.
;;
;; `(deny process-exec*)` cannot be blanket: sandbox-exec applies the profile
;; before exec'ing the interpreter, so denying every exec denies the one that
;; starts the child. The interpreter is allowed by literal path and nothing else
;; is -- which is stricter than allowing the directory, and it is the shape the
;; real build should use with the path passed in rather than hard-coded.
(deny process-exec*)
(allow process-exec (literal "/PYTHON/"))
(deny process-fork)
